  "result": "I fixed the clamping bug. Integer range options with an open bound now clamp to the nearest value inside the range, and the relevant tests pass (71 passed, 2 skipped).\n\n- **The fix:** In `src/click/types.py`, `IntRange._clamp` now returns `bound + dir` instead of `bound - dir`. The old code pushed the value past the bound instead of back inside it. For example, `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-1` now returns `1` instead of `-1`.\n- **Tests:** I added two open-bound clamp cases to `test_range` in `tests/test_types.py`, then ran `tests/test_types.py` and `tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
